{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/697842-killing-blow-with-firearms","id":697842,"title":"killing blow with firearms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-11T13:28:37-07:00","id":697842,"title":"killing blow with firearms","content":"Hi,<br /> I have a question:<br /> A PC has the merit &quot;murder expert&quot; that convert every surprise attack in a killing blow.<br /> Now, he successed in a surprise roll hidden in a second flor flat, and shot in the street below.<br /> For a close combat I don't see any problem in letting him deal a killing blow, but for a long distance (17m) shot??? I mean, he could miss the targhet or not be so precise. I want clarify that he have just 1 dot in firearms so he is not so skilled. <br /> Ho do you handle this situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T13:54:04-07:00","id":697893,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that's 17 meters, not miles. But to be specific, the skill doesn't convert surprise attacks into killing blows, it requires some premeditation.<br /> <br /> Slasher, p127, 'Drawback: You must name your target on the turn before you attack \u2014 you can\u2019t choose to slaughter whoever is slowest that turn.'<br /> <br /> That said, if you let the character have murder expert, they are a murder expert and guns are very good murder weapons, even at range. So providing they met the prerequisites for the usage of the merit, they successfully murdered a person with a gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-11-2015, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T00:44:43-07:00","id":698447,"title":"","content":"17m isn't really that far of a shot for a gun anyway. That's within the shortest range band of all the basic firearms in the game.<br /> <br /> This seems kind of self correcting to me. If you try for ranged shots that get into medium or long range, you'll suffer penalties, that reduce your dice pool, and thus reduce your total damage via killing blow. Depending on your aptitude, and your weapon, you could go from a shot that actually deals a mortal wound to the character, and one that doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:41:17-08:00","id":812760,"title":"","content":"If it's a rifle with a scope, killshot. If it's a shotgun with anything other than slugs, no killshot. If it's a handgun, 50/50.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T07:49:30-08:00","id":817589,"title":"","content":"With one dot of firearms, his killing blow can't be all that powerful either. Top he is doing 7-9 damage. If this is against a Kindred, that is immediately bashing, and more annoying. If it is against a kindred with resilience, it is almost laughable.<br /> <br /> Granted XP expenditures will make it more deadly over time, but this where you get creative as a GM.<br /> <br /> (Assuming Kindred) This person is getting known for their ability to quickly bring down any targets from hiding. Having attention brought on you for being an effective killer suddenly thrusts the character into the possibility of being a hound for the city. Hounds have interesting jobs and suddenly your character who is exceptionally good at surprise combat finds himself dealing with situations that don't always require surprise combat.<br /> <br /> Perhaps he is investigating the disappearance of a young invictus Daeva and runs across the Daevas ghoul, mind broken and gibbering about nonsense(Thoroughly dominated).<br /> <br /> Perhaps he is sent as backup to ensure peace at negotiations between two influential Kindred. If violence breaks out, how does his surprise attack help when everyone is aware he is there?<br /> <br /> In the end, if you allowed the merit, you have to come up with creative solutions to limit it if you feel it is to powerful. Normally I would say allow it, Kindred have for more powerful abilities, and this merit hardly breaks the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:08:01-08:00","id":817671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/697842-killing-blow-with-firearms?p=812760#post812760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's a rifle with a scope, killshot. If it's a shotgun with anything other than slugs, no killshot. If it's a handgun, 50/50.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be missing the point of the original question, which involves a 1e Merit that allows an attacker to use the Killing Blow rules (you succeed with a number of successes equal to your dice-pool instead of roll), on a successful sneak attack. Killing Blow is not a binary, &quot;they're dead if you succeed,&quot; sort of deal. It's just an incredibly powerful attack.<br /> <br /> The specific gun doesn't matter to whether or not the Merit works, because the Merit is about super-vicious sneak attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:33:02-08:00","id":817743,"title":"","content":"I didn't find a specific merit that allow, in 2ED, to deal a Killing Strike. So how it is supposed to works in 2 ed? How can a kindred deal a killing blow? Probably I'm missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:40:37-08:00","id":817755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/697842-killing-blow-with-firearms?p=817671#post817671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems to be missing the point of the original question, which involves a 1e Merit that allows an attacker to use the Killing Blow rules (you succeed with a number of successes equal to your dice-pool instead of roll), on a successful sneak attack. Killing Blow is not a binary, &quot;they're dead if you succeed,&quot; sort of deal. It's just an incredibly powerful attack.<br /> <br /> The specific gun doesn't matter to whether or not the Merit works, because the Merit is about super-vicious sneak attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMy point was accuracy. At a range of 17m, and only 1 dot in firearms, a shotgun(using bird/buckshot) is almost worthless, but if you're using a sniper rifle with a scope, you may as well be right next to them. I would think that makes a big difference in whether or not you can land a Killing Blow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:51:42-08:00","id":817797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/697842-killing-blow-with-firearms?p=817755#post817755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bMy point was accuracy. At a range of 17m, and only 1 dot in firearms, a shotgun(using bird/buckshot) is almost worthless, but if you're using a sniper rifle with a scope, you may as well be right next to them. I would think that makes a big difference in whether or not you can land a Killing Blow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that difference is already represented by the increase in damage due to whatever penalties to the dicepool are being subtracted from damage. So accuracy is pretty much already taken into account.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:53:31-08:00","id":817927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/697842-killing-blow-with-firearms?p=817743#post817743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't find a specific merit that allow, in 2ED, to deal a Killing Strike. So how it is supposed to works in 2 ed? How can a kindred deal a killing blow? Probably I'm missing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing Blows aren't a Merit thing, they're a general combat thing. This is true in 1e and 2e. Anyone can achieve a Killing Blow, since it is how the system models an attack on a target with no hope of doing anything, or anything intervening on their behalf. So a vampire that is simply standing over an unconscious mortal, can claim a Killing Blow on the, unless the ST or another PC does something to intervene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/697842-killing-blow-with-firearms?p=817755#post817755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMy point was accuracy. At a range of 17m, and only 1 dot in firearms, a shotgun(using bird/buckshot) is almost worthless, but if you're using a sniper rifle with a scope, you may as well be right next to them. I would think that makes a big difference in whether or not you can land a Killing Blow.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, again, irrelevant. Killing Blows aren't inherently fatal. If you have 4 dice, and a 0L weapon, you're not killing a healthy human adult with the Killing Blow rules. You're just seriously hurting them (double tap is a thing for a reason...).<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if you have 4 dice because you have Dexterity 3/Firearms 1 and are at short range, or Dexterity 3/Firearms 3 and are at long range.<br /> <br /> Accuracy, and how range impacts it, is built into the Killing Blow rules by potentially reducing the damage done, not be dictating when an attack counts as one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:41:07-08:00","id":817970,"title":"","content":"Right, It just seems to me that being able to <u>target</u> the most vital parts of the body is how you do the <u>most</u> damage, and thus whether or not you <b>Murder </b>someone; In Melee combat, a sledgehammer to the ribs would not be a Killing Blow in my mind, because as bad as that is, it's rarely going to finish the job.(a healthy human being can still stand and fight with broken ribs.) If, on the other hand, that same amount of force was applied to the target's skull, Death or Incapacitation(followed by Death) is a likely outcome. This is more narrative than mechanical, perhaps, but my take on the situation as described by OP remains as follows:\u200b<br /> <br /> Scoped Rifle=Everything about this scenario is in favor of you committing <b>Murder</b>, apply the merit. This amounts to a sneak attack, or attacking someone who is Prone, Bound, or Incapacitated. They realistically have no way of dodging or defending themselves,(not counting Supernatural abilities) so the attack does maximum damage, target should be at least Wounded(Note that a rifle has a rather high damage profile, this adds to the reason for it being a viable <b>Murder</b> weapon in the above scenario.)<br /> <br /> Scattergun=Your weapon is unlikely to <b>Murder</b> under these conditions, do not apply the merit. At 17m, the amount of pellets that would make impact with the target is relatively small, and therefore unlikely to kill, or even seriously wound.<br /> <br /> Handgun/Shotgun with slugs=Sub-optimal conditions for <b>Murder</b>, ST's discretion. You may or may not be able to do a <b>Murderous</b> amount of damage under these conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 01-27-2016, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:51:08-08:00","id":818016,"title":"","content":"And that's exactly what Killing Blow is.. you have the perfect conditions to line up your shot, hence you deal your full dice pool in damage. If your dicepool is small, that might not be enough, shoot twice. If it's big enough, that might be enough. <br /> <br /> People survive grievous wounds... I don't understand the problem here? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:11:15-08:00","id":818108,"title":"","content":"As well, in the OP, the character <b>has a Merit that lets them use the Killing Blow rules</b> when the Merit is triggered. Denying someone access to a Merit's effects because &quot;Eh, I don't think that weapon is 'murderous' enough for that circumstance,&quot; is silly. People try to kill people with all sorts of sub-optimal weapons. Murder is a matter of intent, not equipment.<br /> <br /> It's like saying, &quot;You're playing a chemist with Science 3, a specialty in Chemistry boosted with Area of Expertise, and Professional Training 5 with Science as one of your asset Skills. However, since this science action is more biology than chemistry, you can't use Professional Training's bonuses even though they don't only apply to specializations. Also it doesn't matter that you're rolling two less dice already to represent going out of your character's normal work.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:39:36-08:00","id":821328,"title":"","content":"The real deal here is to understand what the <b>Killing Blow Rule</b> represents, and forget about <u>murder</u> entirely. Yes, the merit had the intent to facilitate kills, and the Killing Blow Rule has such name for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> But it isn't instant kill or a treatise about optimal killing circumstances. It is just about<b></b>: in an optimal condition to use your abilities, you have your entire dice-pool as successes. That's all to begin with. So anything affecting your dice-pool is already affecting your killing blow. That includes weapon range. That includes lack of skill. That includes anything at all that reduces your accuracy, because any reduction in accuracy will reduce your dice-pool, given that it is how the system models accuracy. That aside, anything about actual ability, equipment or the possibility to access the head or the heart is completely irrelevant, not because they aren't issues, but because they are <u><i>already</i></u> taken into account.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if the rule have <b>Killing</b> in the name. If your character have just 3 dice to hit and +2 damage from the weapon, the &quot;Killing Blow&quot; will cause just 5 Lethal and won't even cause penalties to a normal human with Stamina 3.<br /> <br /> So, just use it as it is. The character is a superlative dealer of destruction with surprise. It is a little strong, but is the benefit of the merit, and shouldn't be limited to melee combat. It isn't as strong as it seems, since you actually needs 14 damage to insta-kill the average human (7 Lethal and them 7 aggravated). And to be so superlative at dealing damage shouldn't be that relevant on the game, either.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you're having actual problems with this, for whatever reason (including your campaign being too combat-oriented for this to pass), then just ask the player to change the points for another merit. It is easier and more reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:56:12-08:00","id":821779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems kind of self correcting to me. If you try for ranged shots that get into medium or long range, you'll suffer penalties, that reduce your dice pool, and thus reduce your total damage via killing blow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The math does seem to auto-correct or to rephrase:<br /> <br /> The penalties already applicable makes it balanced from a game view, and makes sense in that the further you are the less effective your ability to murder someone is. Dice penalties translate directly into less actual damage done, not just lost potential damage. In a way, this means the penalties mean more in the face of losing guaranteed damage..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-02-2016, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}